    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d883">

                <pb facs="1178" n="1164" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/12–2344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-23T20:00:00+07:00">December 23,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 25—12:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2062. Political Vice Foreign Minister<anchor n="5" xml:id="d883-f1"/> has
                    informed us that Executive Yuan has recommended to National Defense Council that
                    abolition of Boxer indemnity boards be suspended and that therefore “China
                    Foundation can carry on next year.” (Reurtel 1626, December 12.) We shall expect
                    to obtain additional information and report further in due course.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d883-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
